1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Shido, what's in here?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Is it a date?

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Tell me!

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Upon Toka's arrival in this strange new world,

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
she was immediately faced with a challenge.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
She could choose to fight against the appetite

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
of her growing curiosity,

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
or feed it generously with love.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
And today, Shido's wallet is also feeling conflicted.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
I can answer for more than 8 months later

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The city knows it!

12
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:54,000
We might at all jump on some sort in the dark one

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,800
光求めた瞳

14
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:04,960
後ろは絶望だけ

15
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:09,840
誰にも届かない叫び

16
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:13,820
さあ ツその手で止めて

17
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:16,820
何もかも壊れた世界で

18
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:19,900
理由もわからないままに

19
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:23,640
増えた優しさがまだ

20
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,980
恐くて

21
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:33,440
花のあいた心の隙間 埋めてくれる人は君なの?

22
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:37,360
選んでD landslide

23
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,440
D sympathy

24
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:47,780
ın ad

25
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:48,520
D ko voilà

26
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:54,920
Thank you. Please come again.

27
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:57,800
Here you go.

28
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,560
Is this a test? Am I about to fail?

29
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,980
No, it's for you. Stop drooling.

30
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:16,020
Was this one of those date things?

31
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:17,040
No, it's bread.

32
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:21,120
Okay. Is that another name for date?

33
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:24,200
I don't understand how something so delicious can't be called a date.

34
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,740
You can call it one if you want to.

35
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:30,680
Fascinating. Even though this was delicious, it's still not good enough to be called a date.

36
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,840
And so the mystery continues.

37
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,880
There's one!

38
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:36,980
Not quite.

39
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,220
Oh, he's perfect. Where'd he come from?

40
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,880
Is this one?

41
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:45,760
In the case, I better attack before the Mecca Mecca squad.

42
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,660
No, wait. You don't want to do that.

43
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,560
Why are you stopping me? We're saving us!

44
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:53,040
I'm not. There's nothing to save us from. No one is trying to hurt us.

45
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:56,300
Look, Mama.

46
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,780
See? I threw it in the trash all by myself.

47
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:02,860
Oh, wow. What a good boy you are.

48
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:19,120
What about right now? This moment? Is this a date?

49
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:21,780
Not really, but you're getting closer.

50
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,860
Dates are complicated matters.

51
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:27,940
Look, that thing over there looks yummy!

52
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,380
How in the world are you still hungry?

53
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:32,840
Am I Kray or is that Shida with a new girl?

54
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,380
Oh my gosh, does that mean he's cheating on Tonomachi?

55
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,620
That's so lame.

56
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,600
That woman. I know she's a spirit.

57
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,880
But there's no spatial quake.

58
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:45,180
Sgt. Origami reporting.

59
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:49,340
A-0613. Need an observation device immediately.

60
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,620
No, racist!

61
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:57,660
I can't believe humans eat such amazingly delicious things!

62
00:03:58,780 --> 00:03:59,620
Oh, hey, Toka.

63
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,540
What happened after you left yesterday?

64
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:04,100
Same thing as usual.

65
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,240
I swing my sword around some.

66
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,500
I blast the artillery.

67
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:11,140
In the end, my body disappeared naturally like it always does.

68
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,000
Disappeared?

69
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,660
Yes, I go to a world different from this one.

70
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,040
It's a dark space.

71
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:18,220
Once I get there, I just fall asleep.

72
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:20,800
So you mean when you wake up, you come here?

73
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:23,200
Well, I don't wake up on my own.

74
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,880
It's more like by force.

75
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,380
And it has nothing to do with what I want.

76
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,980
I'm just pulled here, usually anyway.

77
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:30,940
By force?

78
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:34,440
Then spirits don't cause spatial quakes on purpose.

79
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:36,460
They must just be accidents.

80
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,920
By usually, you mean today was different?

81
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:42,420
How would I know?

82
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:43,900
Please tell me.

83
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:47,380
Look, that might actually be the reason there wasn't a spatial quake today.

84
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:48,320
You're too persistent.

85
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,340
Besides, I have important things to do, like find more food.

86
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,280
Toka, come on.

87
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:52,740
Wait.

88
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,780
I should have brought more money.

89
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:59,020
It looks like she's a 98.5% match.

90
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:01,820
That's way too high to be a coincidence, of course.

91
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:03,960
But why is she here?

92
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,720
She isn't wearing her spirit armor right now.

93
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,520
If we want to attack, this is it.

94
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,080
Think about where you are.

95
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,980
You know we can't afford to be reckless.

96
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,240
What kind of place is this?

97
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,960
Uh, an expensive one.

98
00:05:19,180 --> 00:05:20,540
I don't know what that means.

99
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,480
I'm going in.

100
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,560
No, wait, hold on.

101
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,980
Well, if it isn't Shido.

102
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:25,680
Momachi?

103
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:26,520
Hmm?

104
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,240
What do we have here?

105
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:31,060
That's some hot action.

106
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:34,640
How did you manage to pull that kind of tail without me knowing about it, huh?

107
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:36,340
I'm a little jealous.

108
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,580
Yeah, a lot has happened lately, I guess.

109
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,560
Whoa, and straight off the top of the shelf.

110
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:43,080
It's cool, man.

111
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:45,000
My lady's got some pretty expensive tastes, too.

112
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:45,680
Check it out.

113
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,320
Right.

114
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:47,740
His virtual girlfriend.

115
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,420
Listen, I want to help you.

116
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:53,060
Someone gave me these tickets, but I think they'll impress your fancy new girlie and help

117
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:53,920
you score later.

118
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:55,540
You're welcome in advance.

119
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:57,440
Let me know how it goes.

120
00:05:57,900 --> 00:05:58,980
See you later, bud.

121
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,580
How are you today?

122
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:06,240
Reina?

123
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:06,600
What?

124
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:10,700
What are you doing here?

125
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:11,980
Checking on Princess.

126
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:15,300
We have to make sure we're not at risk of another spatial quake.

127
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,560
She's been waiting for you right over there.

128
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:18,880
Over here, Shido!

129
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:20,520
Why are you so late?

130
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:21,780
Sorry.

131
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:25,980
What's up, kitten?

132
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:26,960
You ready to order?

133
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:28,800
Kotari?

134
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:29,360
What?

135
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,420
I couldn't...

136
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,580
Hmm.

137
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:34,340
This looks so good, but so does that one.

138
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:36,760
I wonder which of these two is the date.

139
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,640
Hey, if you guys can't decide, I have a suggestion for you.

140
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,700
But how about this?

141
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,200
What does that one come with?

142
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:44,900
Whoa.

143
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,820
Should be called What's With All This?

144
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:49,680
How?

145
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,300
No, thank you.

146
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,660
It tastes so outrageous.

147
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:54,240
It must be a date.

148
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,360
What are you trying to pull here, Kotari?

149
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:57,820
Thank you works, too.

150
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,320
We're pulling out all the stops to help you score, because I'm awesome.

151
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:02,620
But we also have some business to discuss.

152
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:05,620
As soon as you guys leave, I need you to head south of the station.

153
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,720
But what for?

154
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,620
That's just a residential area.

155
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:09,700
Okay, then.

156
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:11,140
I trust you've got this.

157
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:14,920
Now, let's get this date started.

158
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,960
Checking AI analysis.

159
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,500
Use shop type E-5963.

160
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:23,240
E-5963.

161
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,080
Roger.

162
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,460
Open the main gate.

163
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:36,760
What's that?

164
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:37,840
Let's eat it!

165
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:38,880
It looks so yummy!

166
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,320
No, you can't eat them.

167
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,380
Well, you can, but not those.

168
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,200
Wow, they even have red ones.

169
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:45,360
They're so fast!

170
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:48,000
Yeah, the red ones are three times as fast as the others.

171
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,320
Don't know why they'd be here, though.

172
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,260
The heck is all that?

173
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:55,060
Congratulations!

174
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:59,100
What is going on here?

175
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:02,380
You two are this shopping arcade's 100,000 visitors!

176
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,900
So we have a special gift for both of you!

177
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:07,500
Everything you eat here today will be free!

178
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:09,020
Congratulations!

179
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:11,560
Thanks, but I don't get it.

180
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:13,920
I've never seen one of those before!

181
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,520
Wait, Toka, come back here!

182
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:16,980
Nice work, Kawagui.

183
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:18,560
All right.

184
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,280
Fried food team, get ready for service.

185
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,800
Fish cake and shaved ice team approach customers.

186
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,040
Noodle team, why was the delivery late?

187
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:26,960
Do you think we're going to be okay?

188
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,860
Shin and Toka are moving in.

189
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:31,140
Glad to see we're all ready and prepared for action.

190
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,680
Speak for yourself.

191
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,840
The signal's jammed.

192
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,220
Origami, can you hear me?

193
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:42,540
I've managed to squeeze mobilization orders from the higher-ups.

194
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:44,160
Meet us at point 101.

195
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:45,380
Roger that.

196
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:46,740
Yummy!

197
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:48,640
I can't get over the food!

198
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:49,740
What's that?

199
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:50,720
It looks amazing!

200
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:53,160
Ooh, so does this!

201
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:53,820
Jimmy!

202
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,060
Slow down!

203
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:55,720
Don't rush!

204
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:56,740
Eat as much as you want.

205
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:57,200
It's free.

206
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,540
How the hell did this happen?

207
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:01,300
Shito.

208
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,960
I'm having fun.

209
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:04,720
Are you?

210
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:05,240
Huh?

211
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:09,520
This has been such a great day, and I'm having a wonderful time here.

212
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:11,180
But I'm worried I'm the only one.

213
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,120
You seem upset.

214
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:13,000
Are you mad at me?

215
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:13,460
No way!

216
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,660
Of course I'm not mad at you!

217
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:16,440
Are you sure?

218
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,800
I'm positive.

219
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,540
In fact, I'm in a great mood.

220
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:21,640
I've just had a lot on my mind, is all.

221
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:23,540
Promise you're having a good time?

222
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,400
Best time ever.

223
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,260
I really hope you're telling the truth.

224
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,320
I am, I swear.

225
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:29,160
I'm glad we came here today.

226
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,180
There's so much food we have to try.

227
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:38,400
Let's get the most we can out of the state.

228
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:39,700
Yeah, let's.

229
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:40,780
Great, come on.

230
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:41,000
Okay.

231
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,160
Wherever you need me to go, I'll follow.

232
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,820
Congratulations, you two!

233
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:53,500
You won the grand prize!

234
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:56,140
Two tickets to Dream Park, redeemable any time!

235
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:56,500
Woo!

236
00:09:56,660 --> 00:09:58,960
I don't know what that means, but it sounds like fun!

237
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:00,260
It's the most fun you'll ever have!

238
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:00,860
What's this?

239
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,700
You've never been?

240
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,960
That's unheard of!

241
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,300
You've got to take her right now!

242
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:04,940
Dream Park?

243
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:06,100
Game!

244
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:06,860
Go!

245
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:08,980
Whoa.

246
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,120
Look how beautiful this place is!

247
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:11,980
What an adventure!

248
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:14,060
What kind of things can we do in here?

249
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,920
Well, I don't know.

250
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:17,500
Do it, do it, do it!

251
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:18,560
Hey, I have an idea.

252
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,340
Let's not go in there, okay?

253
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,420
I don't agree.

254
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,960
You told me that we could go wherever I wanted today.

255
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:27,900
Shito, do you think I'll learn what a date is behind those doors?

256
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:29,880
Something tells me that's very possible.

257
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,860
But I don't think it's a good idea today.

258
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,020
Besides when I'm legal.

259
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:34,060
I'm not ready to go yet!

260
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:37,580
How am I supposed to learn if you won't let me experience these things?

261
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,540
Origami, where are you?

262
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,360
What's happening?

263
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:41,960
The time to meet has passed.

264
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:43,660
Currently surveying the movements of the target.

265
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:48,100
Send an emergency arming device to point 088107.

266
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,340
I can't believe I'm seeing this.

267
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,400
Why didn't he bring her in to do the deed?

268
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:04,960
This isn't the first time you've failed with that tactic, is it, Kawagale?

269
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,640
Fact established and acknowledged.

270
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:08,940
Classic Shito.

271
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:12,020
He always insists on doing everything in a proper order.

272
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:13,000
What's that?

273
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:13,900
Rain?

274
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:15,220
Strange.

